{"id":"29b813e9a4475d32850b42f430a0bd1e7ae7d2fb","axis":"silent","repo":"elastic/elasticsearch","sha":"29b813e9a4475d32850b42f430a0bd1e7ae7d2fb","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/changelog/165897.yaml","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@","+area: ES|QL","+issues: []","+pr: 165897","+summary: \"ES|QL|DS: Collect metrics for failed and cancelled external-source queries\"","+type: bug"],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"x-pack/plugin/core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/esql/QueryMetricsListener.java","lines":["@@ -7,20 +7,78 @@"," "," package org.elasticsearch.xpack.core.esql;"," ","+import org.elasticsearch.ExceptionsHelper;","+","+import java.util.List;"," import java.util.Map;"," "," /**","- * Called once per completed ES|QL query on the coordinating node.","+ * Called once per ES|QL query that read federated sources, on the coordinating node, with the {@link Outcome} of the query: it","+ * succeeded, failed or was cancelled.","  * Implementations must be cheap and non-blocking — no I/O, no locks, only atomic operations.","  * <p>","- * Currently, the metrics are only collected when the query has federated sources. The metrics collected are raw","- * profile-based metrics, no computation is performed on them at collection time.","+ * The metrics collected are raw profile-based metrics, no computation is performed on them at collection time. For a query that","+ * did not succeed they hold what is known to have been done before it ended, which can be less than what was done: the work of a","+ * data node that died is not known.","+ * </p>","+ * <p>","+ * A listener that only implements {@link #onQueryCompleted(Map)} is called for the queries that succeeded and for no others, so","+ * that work that was not delivered is not counted by a consumer that does not know about outcomes, such as billing.","+ * A listener that wants every outcome implements {@link #onQueryCompleted(Outcome, Map)}, and implements","+ * {@link #onQueryCompleted(Map)} as well, with nothing to do or an assertion that it is not called: it stays abstract so that","+ * the interface remains a functional interface.","  * </p>","  */"," public interface QueryMetricsListener {"," ","     QueryMetricsListener NOOP = metrics -> {};"," ","+    /**","+     * How a query ended.","+     */","+    enum Outcome {","+        /** The query returned its results. */","+        SUCCESS,","+        /** The query failed, for any reason other than a cancellation. */","+        FAILED,","+        /** The query was cancelled: by the user, because its task was cancelled, or because it expired. */","+        CANCELLED","+    }","+","+    /**","+     * A listener that calls every listener in {@code listeners}, as it is when this is called, in turn, or {@link #NOOP} if there","+     * are none. A listener that throws does not keep the ones after it from being called, which are not to be skipped because of","+     * a listener they have nothing to do with, such as billing: the first exception is thrown at the end, with the others","+     * suppressed.","+     */","+    static QueryMetricsListener composite(List<QueryMetricsListener> listeners) {","+        if (listeners.isEmpty()) {","+            return NOOP;","+        }","+        List<QueryMetricsListener> all = List.copyOf(listeners);","+        return new QueryMetricsListener() {","+            @Override","+            public void onQueryCompleted(Map<String, Long> metrics) {","+                onQueryCompleted(Outcome.SUCCESS, metrics);","+            }","+","+            @Override","+            public void onQueryCompleted(Outcome outcome, Map<String, Long> metrics) {","+                RuntimeException failure = null;","+                for (QueryMetricsListener listener : all) {","+                    try {","+                        listener.onQueryCompleted(outcome, metrics);","+                    } catch (RuntimeException e) {","+                        failure = ExceptionsHelper.useOrSuppress(failure, e);","+                    }","+                }","+                if (failure != null) {","+                    throw failure;","+                }","+            }","+        };","+    }","+","     /**","      * Wall-clock time spent on planning, from queryProfile.planning(). Includes I/O and transport waits: object-store","      * listings and metadata reads, field caps, enrich and inference round trips.","@@ -63,5 +121,19 @@ public interface QueryMetricsListener {","      */","     String BYTES_READ = \"bytes_read\";"," ","+    /**","+     * A query succeeded. Called by the default implementation of {@link #onQueryCompleted(Outcome, Map)}, and only for queries that","+     * succeeded.","+     */","     void onQueryCompleted(Map<String, Long> metrics);","+","+    /**","+     * A query ended with {@code outcome}. The default implementation passes the queries that succeeded to","+     * {@link #onQueryCompleted(Map)} and ignores the others.","+     */","+    default void onQueryCompleted(Outcome outcome, Map<String, Long> metrics) {","+        if (outcome == Outcome.SUCCESS) {","+            onQueryCompleted(metrics);","+        }","+    }"," }"],"additions":75,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"x-pack/plugin/core/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/esql/QueryMetricsListenerTests.java","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,155 @@","+/*","+ * Copyright Elasticsearch B.V. and/or licensed to Elasticsearch B.V. under one","+ * or more contributor license agreements. Licensed under the Elastic License","+ * 2.0; you may not use this file except in compliance with the Elastic License","+ * 2.0.","+ */","+","+package org.elasticsearch.xpack.core.esql;","+","+import org.elasticsearch.test.ESTestCase;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.core.esql.QueryMetricsListener.Outcome;","+","+import java.util.ArrayList;","+import java.util.List;","+import java.util.Map;","+","+import static org.hamcrest.Matchers.equalTo;","+import static org.hamcrest.Matchers.sameInstance;","+","+public class QueryMetricsListenerTests extends ESTestCase {","+","+    /** A consumer that does not know about outcomes, like billing, is never called for a query that did not succeed. */","+    public void testListenerThatIgnoresOutcomesOnlySeesSuccess() {","+        List<Map<String, Long>> seen = new ArrayList<>();","+        QueryMetricsListener listener = seen::add;","+        Map<String, Long> succeeded = Map.of(QueryMetricsListener.CPU_NANOS, 1L);","+","+        listener.onQueryCompleted(Outcome.FAILED, Map.of(QueryMetricsListener.CPU_NANOS, 2L));","+        listener.onQueryCompleted(Outcome.CANCELLED, Map.of(QueryMetricsListener.CPU_NANOS, 3L));","+        listener.onQueryCompleted(Outcome.SUCCESS, succeeded);","+","+        assertThat(seen.size(), equalTo(1));","+        assertThat(seen.get(0), sameInstance(succeeded));","+    }","+","+    public void testListenerThatKnowsOutcomesSeesAllOfThem() {","+        List<Outcome> seen = new ArrayList<>();","+        QueryMetricsListener listener = new QueryMetricsListener() {","+            @Override","+            public void onQueryCompleted(Map<String, Long> metrics) {","+                fail(\"outcomes are delivered with the outcome\");","+            }","+","+            @Override","+            public void onQueryCompleted(Outcome outcome, Map<String, Long> metrics) {","+                seen.add(outcome);","+            }","+        };","+","+        for (Outcome outcome : Outcome.values()) {","+            listener.onQueryCompleted(outcome, Map.of());","+        }","+","+        assertThat(seen, equalTo(List.of(Outcome.values())));","+    }","+","+    public void testCompositeOfNothingIsNoop() {","+        assertThat(QueryMetricsListener.composite(List.of()), sameInstance(QueryMetricsListener.NOOP));","+    }","+","+    public void testCompositeCallsEveryListenerWithTheOutcomeAndRespectsEachOnesChoice() {","+        List<Outcome> outcomeAware = new ArrayList<>();","+        List<Outcome> successOnly = new ArrayList<>();","+        QueryMetricsListener aware = new QueryMetricsListener() {","+            @Override","+            public void onQueryCompleted(Map<String, Long> metrics) {","+                fail(\"outcomes are delivered with the outcome\");","+            }","+","+            @Override","+            public void onQueryCompleted(Outcome outcome, Map<String, Long> metrics) {","+                outcomeAware.add(outcome);","+            }","+        };","+        QueryMetricsListener unaware = metrics -> successOnly.add(Outcome.SUCCESS);","+        QueryMetricsListener composite = QueryMetricsListener.composite(List.of(aware, unaware));","+","+        composite.onQueryCompleted(Outcome.FAILED, Map.of());","+        composite.onQueryCompleted(Outcome.SUCCESS, Map.of());","+        composite.onQueryCompleted(Outcome.CANCELLED, Map.of());","+","+        assertThat(outcomeAware, equalTo(List.of(Outcome.FAILED, Outcome.SUCCESS, Outcome.CANCELLED)));","+        assertThat(successOnly, equalTo(List.of(Outcome.SUCCESS)));","+    }","+","+    /** What a consumer written before outcomes existed looks like: a class that implements the one method it was given. */","+    private static final class SuccessSumListener implements QueryMetricsListener {","+        long sum;","+","+        @Override","+        public void onQueryCompleted(Map<String, Long> metrics) {","+            sum += metrics.get(QueryMetricsListener.CPU_NANOS);","+        }","+    }","+","+    public void testListenerWrittenBeforeOutcomesCountsOnlySuccessThroughTheComposite() {","+        SuccessSumListener old = new SuccessSumListener();","+        QueryMetricsListener composite = QueryMetricsListener.composite(List.of(old));","+","+        composite.onQueryCompleted(Outcome.FAILED, Map.of(QueryMetricsListener.CPU_NANOS, 100L));","+        composite.onQueryCompleted(Outcome.SUCCESS, Map.of(QueryMetricsListener.CPU_NANOS, 7L));","+        composite.onQueryCompleted(Outcome.CANCELLED, Map.of(QueryMetricsListener.CPU_NANOS, 1000L));","+","+        assertThat(old.sum, equalTo(7L));","+    }","+","+    /** A listener that throws, such as one that only monitors, must not keep the ones after it, such as billing, from being called. */","+    public void testCompositeCallsTheOtherListenersWhenOneThrowsAndThrowsTheFirstFailure() {","+        List<String> called = new ArrayList<>();","+        QueryMetricsListener first = metrics -> called.add(\"first\");","+        IllegalStateException brokenFailure = new IllegalStateException(\"broken\");","+        QueryMetricsListener broken = metrics -> { throw brokenFailure; };","+        IllegalArgumentException anotherFailure = new IllegalArgumentException(\"another\");","+        QueryMetricsListener another = metrics -> { throw anotherFailure; };","+        QueryMetricsListener last = metrics -> called.add(\"last\");","+        QueryMetricsListener composite = QueryMetricsListener.composite(List.of(first, broken, another, last));","+","+        IllegalStateException thrown = expectThrows(","+            IllegalStateException.class,","+            () -> composite.onQueryCompleted(Outcome.SUCCESS, Map.of())","+        );","+","+        assertThat(thrown, sameInstance(brokenFailure));","+        assertThat(thrown.getSuppressed(), equalTo(new Throwable[] { anotherFailure }));","+        assertThat(called, equalTo(List.of(\"first\", \"last\")));","+    }","+","+    public void testCompositeIsNotAffectedByLaterChangesToItsList() {","+        List<QueryMetricsListener> listeners = new ArrayList<>();","+        List<String> called = new ArrayList<>();","+        listeners.add(metrics -> called.add(\"first\"));","+        QueryMetricsListener composite = QueryMetricsListener.composite(listeners);","+        listeners.add(metrics -> called.add(\"added later\"));","+","+        composite.onQueryCompleted(Outcome.SUCCESS, Map.of());","+","+        assertThat(called, equalTo(List.of(\"first\")));","+    }","+","+    /** The composite also stands in for listeners called the old way. */","+    public void testCompositeCalledWithoutOutcomeIsASuccess() {","+        List<Outcome> seen = new ArrayList<>();","+        QueryMetricsListener aware = new QueryMetricsListener() {","+            @Override","+            public void onQueryCompleted(Map<String, Long> metrics) {}","+","+            @Override","+            public void onQueryCompleted(Outcome outcome, Map<String, Long> metrics) {","+                seen.add(outcome);","+            }","+        };","+        QueryMetricsListener.composite(List.of(aware)).onQueryCompleted(Map.of());","+        assertThat(seen, equalTo(List.of(Outcome.SUCCESS)));","+    }","+}"],"additions":155,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/compute/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/compute/operator/Driver.java","lines":["@@ -89,8 +89,8 @@ public class Driver implements Releasable, Describable {","     private final List<OperatorStatus> statusOfCompletedOperators = new ArrayList<>();","     /**","      * Operators that asked to be resnapshotted after {@code waitForAsyncActions}. Index is into","-     * {@link #statusOfCompletedOperators}. Mutated only after {@link #isFinished()} when the","-     * driver loop is dead.","+     * {@link #statusOfCompletedOperators}. Mutated only when the driver loop is dead: once the driver is finished, or","+     * when it fails or is aborted and drains its operators.","      */","     private final List<PendingFinalStatus> pendingFinalStatus = new ArrayList<>();","     private final Releasable releasable;","@@ -241,8 +241,10 @@ public DriverContext driverContext() {","      * this runs inside an operator's measurement of this driver. That happens once the driver was cancelled or finished","      * early: the scheduler then runs it directly on the thread that completes the listener it is blocked on, such as a","      * worker's.","-     * CPU and driver time are published at status updates. If an iteration throws, including cancellation,","-     * time accumulated since the last status update is not included in the reported totals.","+     * CPU and driver time are published at status updates. If an iteration throws, including cancellation, the driver","+     * still publishes a final status, with the status of its operators, once it has drained them. That status includes the","+     * CPU time of the failed iteration, which is committed when its measurement closes, but not the CPU time of draining","+     * and closing the operators afterwards, nor the driver time since the last status update.","      */","     SubscribableListener<Void> run(TimeValue maxTime, int maxIterations, LongSupplier currentTimeNanosSupplier) {","         // the driver charges its own time, and its pool the rest of the task to the load target","@@ -383,7 +385,13 @@ public void abort(Exception reason, ActionListener<Void> listener) {","         completionListener.addListener(listener);","         if (started.compareAndSet(false, true)) {","             drainAndCloseOperators(reason);","-            completionListener.onFailure(reason);","+            try {","+                // Unlike the failure of a running driver, abort does not wait for asynchronous actions: operators with","+                // off-driver work are read again now, not after it.","+                publishFinalStatus();","+            } finally {","+                completionListener.onFailure(reason);","+            }","         } else {","             cancel(reason.getMessage());","         }","@@ -496,7 +504,13 @@ protected int closeEarlyFinishedOperators(","                             reportedByClosedSource = now - lastStatusUpdate;","                         }","                     }","-                    op.close();","+                    try {","+                        op.close();","+                    } catch (RuntimeException e) {","+                        // The operator stays active, so the failure's drain closes it again and records its status then.","+                        statusOfCompletedOperators.remove(statusIndex);","+                        throw e;","+                    }","                     if (op.finalStatusAfterAsyncActions()) {","                         pendingFinalStatus.add(new PendingFinalStatus(statusIndex, op));","                     }","@@ -621,7 +635,13 @@ protected void drainAndCloseOperators(@Nullable Exception e) {","         Iterator<Operator> itr = activeOperators.iterator();","         while (itr.hasNext()) {","             try {","-                Releasables.closeWhileHandlingException(itr.next());","+                Operator op = itr.next();","+                if (e != null) {","+                    // The driver failed or was aborted: keep what the operator did, as the early-finish path does but","+                    // tolerating a failing status, so the failed driver still reports its usage. A plain close() does not.","+                    recordStatusBeforeClose(op);","+                }","+                Releasables.closeWhileHandlingException(op);","             } catch (Exception x) {","                 if (e != null) {","                     e.addSuppressed(x);","@@ -633,6 +653,26 @@ protected void drainAndCloseOperators(@Nullable Exception e) {","         Releasables.closeWhileHandlingException(releasable, driverContext.getSnapshot());","     }"," ","+    /**","+     * Adds the status of an operator that is about to be closed without having finished, because the driver failed or was","+     * cancelled. This must never throw: the operator still has to be closed and the failure that is being handled must not","+     * be hidden, so an operator whose status cannot be read is recorded without one.","+     */","+    private void recordStatusBeforeClose(Operator op) {","+        int statusIndex = statusOfCompletedOperators.size();","+        try {","+            statusOfCompletedOperators.add(new OperatorStatus(op.toString(), op.status()));","+            if (op.finalStatusAfterAsyncActions()) {","+                pendingFinalStatus.add(new PendingFinalStatus(statusIndex, op));","+            }","+        } catch (Exception statusFailure) {","+            LOGGER.debug(\"failed to read the status of an operator that is being closed [{}]\", shortDescription, statusFailure);","+            if (statusOfCompletedOperators.size() == statusIndex) {","+                statusOfCompletedOperators.add(new OperatorStatus(op.getClass().getSimpleName(), null));","+            }","+        }","+    }","+","     private static void schedule(","         TimeValue maxTime,","         int maxIterations,","@@ -676,10 +716,15 @@ protected void doRun() {","             public void onFailure(Exception e) {","                 driver.drainAndCloseOperators(e);","                 driver.driverContext.waitForAsyncActions(","-                    ContextPreservingActionListener.wrapPreservingContext(","-                        ActionListener.running(() -> listener.onFailure(e)),","-                        threadContext","-                    )","+                    ContextPreservingActionListener.wrapPreservingContext(ActionListener.running(() -> {","+                        try {","+                            // A failed driver is finished too: publish what it did so the caller can account for it.","+                            driver.finishNanos = System.nanoTime();","+                            driver.publishFinalStatus();","+                        } finally {","+                            listener.onFailure(e);","+                        }","+                    }), threadContext)","                 );","             }"," ","@@ -795,7 +840,12 @@ private void reportSearchLoad(long extraDriverNanos, long now) {","     private void publishFinalStatus() {","         for (PendingFinalStatus pending : pendingFinalStatus) {","             Operator op = pending.operator;","-            statusOfCompletedOperators.set(pending.index, operatorStatus(op));","+            try {","+                statusOfCompletedOperators.set(pending.index, operatorStatus(op));","+            } catch (Exception statusFailure) {","+                // Keep the status taken before the close: failing to refresh it must not leave the driver unfinished.","+                LOGGER.debug(\"failed to re-read the status of a closed operator [{}]\", shortDescription, statusFailure);","+            }","         }","         pendingFinalStatus.clear();","         updateStatus(0, 0, DriverStatus.Status.DONE, \"driver done\", System.nanoTime());","@@ -824,6 +874,12 @@ private void updateStatus(long extraDriverNanos, int extraIterations, DriverStat","             // Sorry for the complexity here. If anyone has a nice way to refactor this, be my guest.","             switch (status) {","                 case ASYNC, WAITING -> sleeps = sleeps.sleep(reason, now);","+                case DONE -> {","+                    // A driver whose blocked future failed ends while asleep: close the sleep, as running again would.","+                    switch (prev.status()) {","+                        case ASYNC, WAITING -> sleeps = sleeps.wake(now);","+                    }","+                }","                 case RUNNING -> {","                     switch (prev.status()) {","                         case ASYNC, WAITING -> sleeps = sleeps.wake(now);"],"additions":68,"deletions":12,"truncated":false},{"path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/compute/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/compute/operator/DriverTests.java","lines":["@@ -10,12 +10,14 @@"," import org.apache.logging.log4j.Level;"," import org.apache.lucene.index.IndexReader;"," import org.elasticsearch.ElasticsearchStatusException;","+import org.elasticsearch.TransportVersion;"," import org.elasticsearch.action.ActionListener;"," import org.elasticsearch.action.ActionRunnable;"," import org.elasticsearch.action.support.PlainActionFuture;"," import org.elasticsearch.action.support.SubscribableListener;"," import org.elasticsearch.common.breaker.CircuitBreaker;"," import org.elasticsearch.common.breaker.CircuitBreakingException;","+import org.elasticsearch.common.io.stream.StreamOutput;"," import org.elasticsearch.common.settings.Settings;"," import org.elasticsearch.common.unit.ByteSizeValue;"," import org.elasticsearch.common.util.MockBigArrays;","@@ -50,6 +52,7 @@"," import org.elasticsearch.threadpool.FixedExecutorBuilder;"," import org.elasticsearch.threadpool.TestThreadPool;"," import org.elasticsearch.threadpool.ThreadPool;","+import org.elasticsearch.xcontent.XContentBuilder;"," "," import java.io.IOException;"," import java.util.ArrayDeque;","@@ -69,10 +72,12 @@"," import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicLong;"," import java.util.function.LongSupplier;"," ","+import static org.hamcrest.Matchers.both;"," import static org.hamcrest.Matchers.either;"," import static org.hamcrest.Matchers.equalTo;"," import static org.hamcrest.Matchers.greaterThan;"," import static org.hamcrest.Matchers.greaterThanOrEqualTo;","+import static org.hamcrest.Matchers.lessThan;"," import static org.hamcrest.Matchers.lessThanOrEqualTo;"," import static org.hamcrest.Matchers.not;"," import static org.hamcrest.Matchers.sameInstance;","@@ -1277,6 +1282,394 @@ public void close() {","         }","     }"," ","+    /**","+     * A driver that fails publishes what its operators did, so the caller can account for the work of a query that failed.","+     * The failed driver is finished: its profile has a valid duration.","+     */","+    public void testFailedDriverPublishesOperatorUsage() {","+        DriverContext driverContext = driverContext();","+        long bytesRead = randomLongBetween(1, 1_000_000);","+        Driver driver = TestDriverFactory.create(","+            driverContext,","+            new UsageSourceOperator(driverContext, new UsageStatus(bytesRead, 11, 7), false),","+            List.of(failingOperator(new IllegalStateException(\"boom\"))),","+            new TestResultPageSinkOperator(page -> fail(\"sink should not receive output\"))","+        );","+        ThreadPool threadPool = threadPool();","+        try {","+            PlainActionFuture<Void> future = new PlainActionFuture<>();","+            Driver.start(threadPool.getThreadContext(), threadPool.executor(\"esql\"), driver, between(1, 1000), future);","+            IllegalStateException failure = expectThrows(IllegalStateException.class, () -> future.actionGet(30, TimeUnit.SECONDS));","+            assertThat(failure.getMessage(), equalTo(\"boom\"));","+            assertFinishedWithUsage(driver, bytesRead, 11, 7);","+            assertThat(driver.profile().tookNanos(), both(greaterThanOrEqualTo(0L)).and(lessThan(TimeUnit.MINUTES.toNanos(1))));","+        } finally {","+            driver.close();","+            terminate(threadPool);","+        }","+    }","+","+    /**","+     * A source whose final status is only known once its asynchronous actions are done, like an external source whose producer","+     * threads are still running when the driver fails: the driver waits for them and reads its status again after them.","+     */","+    public void testFailedDriverWaitsForAsyncActionsAndRereadsStatus() {","+        DriverContext driverContext = driverContext();","+        driverContext.addAsyncAction();","+        UsageSourceOperator source = new UsageSourceOperator(driverContext, new UsageStatus(1, 1, 1), true);","+        Driver driver = TestDriverFactory.create(","+            driverContext,","+            source,","+            List.of(failingOperator(new IllegalStateException(\"boom\"))),","+            new TestResultPageSinkOperator(page -> fail(\"sink should not receive output\"))","+        );","+        ThreadPool threadPool = threadPool();","+        try {","+            PlainActionFuture<Void> future = new PlainActionFuture<>();","+            Driver.start(threadPool.getThreadContext(), threadPool.executor(\"esql\"), driver, between(1, 1000), future);","+            assertBusy(() -> assertTrue(source.closed));","+            // The producer is still running: the failure is not reported and the driver is not finished.","+            assertFalse(future.isDone());","+            assertThat(driver.status().status(), not(equalTo(DriverStatus.Status.DONE)));","+","+            source.producerDone = true;","+            driverContext.removeAsyncAction();","+            expectThrows(IllegalStateException.class, () -> future.actionGet(30, TimeUnit.SECONDS));","+            // Only the read after the asynchronous actions sees the work the producer did in the meantime.","+            assertFinishedWithUsage(driver, 1_000, 1, 1);","+        } catch (Exception e) {","+            throw new AssertionError(e);","+        } finally {","+            driver.close();","+            terminate(threadPool);","+        }","+    }","+","+    /** An operator whose close() fails must not be counted twice: the failing driver closes it again and records it then. */","+    public void testOperatorFailingToCloseIsCountedOnce() {","+        DriverContext driverContext = driverContext();","+        AtomicInteger closeCalls = new AtomicInteger();","+        UsageSourceOperator source = new UsageSourceOperator(driverContext, new UsageStatus(40, 4, 2), false) {","+            @Override","+            public void close() {","+                super.close();","+                if (closeCalls.getAndIncrement() == 0) {","+                    throw new IllegalStateException(\"close failed\");","+                }","+            }","+        };","+        List<Page> outPages = new ArrayList<>();","+        Driver driver = TestDriverFactory.create(driverContext, source, List.of(), new TestResultPageSinkOperator(outPages::add));","+        ThreadPool threadPool = threadPool();","+        try {","+            PlainActionFuture<Void> future = new PlainActionFuture<>();","+            Driver.start(threadPool.getThreadContext(), threadPool.executor(\"esql\"), driver, between(1, 1000), future);","+            IllegalStateException failure = expectThrows(IllegalStateException.class, () -> future.actionGet(30, TimeUnit.SECONDS));","+            assertThat(failure.getMessage(), equalTo(\"close failed\"));","+            assertThat(closeCalls.get(), equalTo(2));","+            // The source and the sink, once each.","+            assertThat(driver.status().completedOperators().size(), equalTo(2));","+            assertFinishedWithUsage(driver, 40, 4, 2);","+        } finally {","+            outPages.forEach(Page::releaseBlocks);","+            driver.close();","+            terminate(threadPool);","+        }","+    }","+","+    /** A driver whose blocked future fails ends while asleep: the sleep must be closed, not reported as still going. */","+    public void testDriverFailingWhileBlockedClosesItsSleep() {","+        DriverContext driverContext = driverContext();","+        SubscribableListener<Void> blocked = new SubscribableListener<>();","+        UsageSourceOperator source = new UsageSourceOperator(driverContext, new UsageStatus(3, 0, 0), false) {","+            @Override","+            public Page getOutput() {","+                return null;","+            }","+","+            @Override","+            public boolean isFinished() {","+                return false;","+            }","+","+            @Override","+            public IsBlockedResult isBlocked() {","+                return new IsBlockedResult(blocked, \"test blocked\");","+            }","+        };","+        Driver driver = TestDriverFactory.create(","+            driverContext,","+            source,","+            List.of(),","+            new TestResultPageSinkOperator(page -> fail(\"sink should not receive output\"))","+        );","+        ThreadPool threadPool = threadPool();","+        try {","+            PlainActionFuture<Void> future = new PlainActionFuture<>();","+            Driver.start(threadPool.getThreadContext(), threadPool.executor(\"esql\"), driver, between(1, 1000), future);","+            assertBusy(() -> assertThat(driver.status().status(), equalTo(DriverStatus.Status.ASYNC)));","+            blocked.onFailure(new IllegalStateException(\"blocked failed\"));","+            IllegalStateException failure = expectThrows(IllegalStateException.class, () -> future.actionGet(30, TimeUnit.SECONDS));","+            assertThat(failure.getMessage(), equalTo(\"blocked failed\"));","+            assertFinishedWithUsage(driver, 3, 0, 0);","+            DriverSleeps.Sleep sleep = driver.status().sleeps().last().get(0);","+            assertThat(sleep.reason(), equalTo(\"test blocked\"));","+            assertFalse(sleep.isStillSleeping());","+        } catch (Exception e) {","+            throw new AssertionError(e);","+        } finally {","+            driver.close();","+            terminate(threadPool);","+        }","+    }","+","+    /** Closing a driver that never ran only releases its operators: it does not read their status, as a failing driver does. */","+    public void testClosingDriverThatNeverRanDoesNotReadOperatorStatus() {","+        DriverContext driverContext = driverContext();","+        AtomicInteger statusReads = new AtomicInteger();","+        UsageSourceOperator source = new UsageSourceOperator(driverContext, new UsageStatus(7, 1, 1), false) {"],"additions":151,"deletions":0,"truncated":false}],"additions":454,"deletions":15,"truncated":true,"file_count":5},"error":null,"fetched_at":"2026-11-18T16:51:38.172672+00:00"}